INSERT INTO "programs"."program_messages" ("id", "day", "title", "subtitle", "body", "program", "question_id", "question_response", "resources", "claire_prompts", "journal_prompts", "meditation", "page_info", "stage", "guide_id") VALUES ('1', '0', '🧘‍♂️ Preparation', 'Get Ready for Clear30!', 'You’re about to start a powerful 30-day journey to take control of your habits. Clear30 is all about making small, consistent changes that lead to big results. 🌱

Quick Tips for Success:
 • Check in daily: Take just a few minutes each day to reflect on your goal, whether it’s during a quiet moment or while brushing your teeth. 🧠
 • Lean on support: Invite a friend to join you or reach out to us for help when you need it. 💪
 • Stay flexible: Use the tips that work for you, but keep an open mind—you never know when something will click. 🔄

Remember, you’ve already taken the first step by committing to this break. You’ve got this, and we’re here to support you every step of the way! 💚.', 'clear30', null, null, '{"The Problem With Weed...":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=NqtYZJSGeEY","Addiction Mindset: T-Breaks":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Zg8mYYwbA1I","Weedless Guide to Preparation":"https://www.weedless.org/guide/","Taking a break is hard! Any suggestions?":"https://www.reddit.com/r/canadients/comments/5yylas/taking_a_break_is_hard_any_suggestions/","Mcwell: Self help guide for 30 day T-break":"https://mcwell.nd.edu/your-well-being/physical-well-being/drugs/marijuana-or-cannabis-sativa/quitting-marijuana-a-30-day-self-help-guide/","UVM: T-Break Preparation (and Guide): Definitely Check it out":"https://www.uvm.edu/health/day-0-preparation"}', '{"🌿 Ease Withdrawal: Your Action Plan 🌟":"Clairebot, based on my profile, guide me in crafting a detailed action plan with daily routines, activities, and habits to ease withdrawal symptoms in Clear30.","🎨 New Free Time? Discover New Habits 🏃":"Can you guide me in either finding a habit worth building or putting into practice a habit I’ve committed to?","👥 Environment Curation: Find Your Place & People 🌎":"Help me manage environmental triggers and identifying and minimizing settings that lead to cravings based on my profile?"}', '["What steps are you taking to prepare for your Clear30?"]', '{"Preparation Meditation":"https://m.clear30.org/preparation.mp3"}', '[{"body":"What if just taking a few minutes a day could change your life? That’s all it takes to start making real, lasting progress on your Clear30 journey. Whether it’s during a quiet moment in the morning, brushing your teeth, or even while you’re on the toilet, checking in with your goal for a few moments can make all the difference. 🚀","title":"🕰️ Start Strong: Small Daily Steps Lead to Big Wins"},{"body":"Clear30 isn’t just about stopping weed—it’s a chance to reinvent yourself. Over the next 30 days, you’ll have the tools to take control, not just of this one habit, but of any challenge you set your mind to. By aligning with the version of yourself you want to be, you’re not only breaking free from weed—you’re building resilience and practicing the art of doing hard things.\\nThink of it this way: Every day you stay committed to this break, you’re casting votes for the person you want to become. 🎯 And by the end of these 30 days, you’ll have not just hit your goal, but also strengthened your ability to tackle bigger goals beyond Clear30.","title":"🧠 Reinvent Yourself, One Step at a Time"},{"body":"You don’t have to go through this alone. In fact, starting Clear30 with a friend can be a game-changer. When you’ve got someone walking the same path as you, it’s easier to stay accountable and support each other. The break with friends option makes it easy to invite someone into the program with you. 💪\\nBut whether you do it with a friend or on your own, we’re here for you. Through online support, you can connect with our team, including Dr. Fred, for that extra bit of encouragement. Sometimes, just knowing there’s someone out there rooting for you makes all the difference.","title":"👥 Lean on Support—From Friends or From Us"},{"body":"One of the biggest challenges people face is staying consistent over time. That’s why we encourage you to make a habit of checking in daily. Whether it’s reading the daily message, reflecting on your goals, or thinking about your progress, setting aside just a few minutes can keep you on track.\\nHere’s a tip: Pair your check-in with a habit you already have. Maybe it’s while you’re brushing your teeth in the morning, or during a moment of downtime. The easier it is to fit into your routine, the more likely you’ll stick with it—and those small, daily actions add up in a big way. 🧩","title":"🎯 Consistency is Key: Check In Every Day"},{"body":"We’re going to be sending a lot of information and strategies your way over the next 30 days. Some things will resonate with you, while others might not. And that’s okay. You don’t have to follow every piece of advice perfectly. Take what works for you and run with it.\\nBut even for the strategies that don’t feel like they apply right away—keep them in the back of your mind. You never know when something you’ve learned might come in handy later on. Sometimes, the most unexpected advice turns out to be exactly what you need down the line.","title":"🔄 Take What Works, Leave the Rest—But Keep an Open Mind"},{"body":"You’re about to do something that’s not easy—and that’s what makes it so powerful. Nobody’s forcing you to take this break. You’re doing it for yourself. That alone says so much about the kind of person you are—someone who is willing to step out of their comfort zone, take on challenges, and grow stronger from them. 🔥\\nThis mindset is going to carry you far—not just through Clear30, but through life. So go in with excitement and an open mind. Whether it’s tough or smooth, the fact that you’re here, trying, is a win in itself. You’ve already taken the hardest step by deciding to make a change.","title":"🌱 Embrace the Challenge"},{"body":"You’ve set the stage for something great. Clear30 is your chance not only to break a habit but to create a stronger version of yourself. Lean on support when you need it, stay consistent with those small daily steps, and keep an open mind. You’re not just stopping weed—you’re proving to yourself that you can do difficult things, and that strength will carry you to bigger, better places.\\nWe’re excited for what’s ahead—and remember, we’re here with you every step of the way. 💚","title":"🔑 Key Takeaway: You’ve Got This—And You’re Already on Your Way"}]', 'withdrawal', null),
('113', '0', '🚀 Welcome to The Life Program', 'Building healthy habits', 'This program is here to help you moderate your weed use while focusing on staying accountable and building healthy habits. 🌱 

You’ll receive daily tips and strategies to guide you through life’s ups and downs, with a focus on overall growth—not just weed. 🧠

If you ever want a structured break, you can always start a Clear30. But for now, this program will keep you motivated and moving forward every day. 💡

Expect:
🕒 Routines to keep you grounded
💪 Mindset shifts for continuous growth
🌍 Real stories and insights to inspire you

Let’s keep moving forward, one day at a time. You’ve got this', 'life', null, null, '{"21 Tiny Habits to Improve Your Life":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ZXTy_dKwMa0&feature=youtu.be","📜 A short guide to a better life.":"https://www.reddit.com/r/selfimprovement/comments/oenml0/a_short_guide_to_a_better_life/"}', '{"🔑 Start Your Path to Progress":"Hey Claire, I want to make some changes and improve, but I’m not sure where to start. Can you help me figure out what might be holding me back and what small habit I could work on first?"}', '["What is one small habit or action you could start today that would have a big positive impact on your life over time?"]', null, '[{"body":"Imagine this: You’re standing at the edge of a life you know you could be living—the healthier, more focused, more fulfilled version of yourself. But something’s holding you back. Maybe it’s your daily routine, your comfort zone, or even just the idea that it’s too late to start. Sound familiar?.\\nHere’s the truth: most people fall short not because they lack potential, but because they get stuck in the rhythm of their everyday lives. Habits and distractions keep us playing small, when deep down, we all want more.","title":"Unlock Your Potential: Why Getting Better Matters"},{"body":"It’s natural to struggle with this stuff. It’s what makes us human. The odds are often not in our favor. The gap between knowing what you need to do and actually taking action is part of the human experience.\\n💡 Why?\\nBecause evolution programs us to conserve energy, and today’s world takes advantage of that. Companies have leveraged our biological wants—sex, comfort, calories—to capture our attention and money, using our instincts against us.\\nBut here’s where you come in: it takes consistent focus and intention to swim against the tide of these forces. And that’s exactly what this program is here to help you with","title":"The Struggle is Real—and Human"},{"body":"There are a few common traps that people fall into when they try to improve:\\n🛋️ Comfort zones: Our routines feel safe, but they often prevent us from growing.\\n⏳ Short-term thinking: People get caught up in immediate gratification and miss out on long-term progress.\\n🏆 Perfectionism: Many quit because they think the journey is about perfection, not improvement.\\n😨 Fear of failure: The idea of trying and not succeeding can be paralyzing.\\n⚠️ But you don’t have to fall into these traps! This program will give you the tools and insights you need to make small, meaningful progress every day.","title":"Why Do So Many Fail?"},{"body":"We’ve gathered wisdom from all over—from philosophers thousands of years ago to Reddit users in 2024 sharing their real-life experiences on what works for them.\\nOur goal is simple:\\nWe want to give you timeless, practical tools that can make a real difference in your life.\\nHere’s what to expect:\\n🕒 Routines that work: How to structure your day for success without feeling overwhelmed.\\n💡 Mindset shifts: From ancient philosophies to modern psychological insights.\\n🌍 Real stories from real people: What works in the real world, from people just like you.\\n🗝️ You don’t need to be the best. You just need to start—and commit to improving little by little.","title":"What You’ll Get from This Program"},{"body":"If you ever want to take a structured 30-day break from weed, you can start a Clear30. Otherwise, this program (either weed-free or moderation mode) will help you with your goals, and the messages will be more geared around you and less about getting through a weed break.","title":"How to Use This Program"}]', 'foundations', null);